From: Tab5 AFC bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] mbedtls: accept empty X.509 Name

Apple's lockdown pair records use self-signed certificates whose subject
and issuer RDNSequence is empty. RFC 5280 permits an empty Name, but
mbedTLS 3.6's mbedtls_x509_get_name() treats the empty SEQUENCE as
truncated and fails with MBEDTLS_ERR_X509_INVALID_NAME +
MBEDTLS_ERR_ASN1_OUT_OF_DATA. That prevents parsing both the host root
certificate used as the TLS client identity and the device certificate
sent by lockdownd.

Accept an empty Name sequence by returning success before the SET loop.

Apply from the ESP-IDF root:
  git apply /home/ops/iap2tab5/tools/mbedtls-empty-name.patch

diff --git a/components/mbedtls/mbedtls/library/x509.c b/components/mbedtls/mbedtls/library/x509.c
--- a/components/mbedtls/mbedtls/library/x509.c
+++ b/components/mbedtls/mbedtls/library/x509.c
@@ -500,6 +500,12 @@ int mbedtls_x509_get_name(unsigned char **p, const unsigned char *end,
     const unsigned char *end_set;
     mbedtls_x509_name *head = cur;
 
+    /* Apple lockdown certificates use an empty subject/issuer Name.
+     * RFC 5280 allows an empty RDNSequence. */
+    if (*p == end) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     /* don't use recursion, we'd risk stack overflow if not optimized */
     while (1) {
         /*
